Remove the --gamma flag from our calls to frecon (which doesn't implement it) and ply-image (which I don't think we use anymore).  BUG=chromium:649739 TEST=none  Change-Id: I59a5bd11b378028d3c6da83e1b8e8e0147a2dd6e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388742 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="388742" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/42/388742/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie7ff513be600693fcefed7c60c9d860fa7b83268" commit="e059a2bfa55662e30034665a198e53b1f263ad10" commit_message="Remove hard coded list of USB_DEVS.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55411 TEST=Installed factory image on device, booted and installed from usb.  Change-Id: Ie7ff513be600693fcefed7c60c9d860fa7b83268 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/375397 Commit-Ready: Alexis Savery &lt;asavery@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alexis Savery &lt;asavery@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="375397" owner_email="asavery@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/initramfs" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/initramfs" ref="refs/changes/97/375397/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I4d645efd1b6294e4a07d353e97945bc12e5a5c5e" commit="9d726ca8e9f7daa72826da717ef8a02cdb03b408" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ALSA: pcm: Fix avail to return error if stream is suspended  When the stream is in suspended state some applications wait on &quot;Stream Pipe Error&quot; in response to snd_pcm_avail call to resume the stream.  In the current implementation snd_pcm_avail() returns zero when the stream is in suspended state. This causes application to enter in infinite loop for frames to be available.  &quot;Stream pipe Error&quot; code is getting returned for read/write call when the stream is in suspended state. Similarly update snd_pcm_avail to return -ESTRPIPE.  Link: git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/tiwai/sound.git tag: v4.8-rc1-31-gf3f6c61 (cherry picked from commit f3f6c61452e28ffdf93b101555546af8ef63def5) Signed-off-by: Jeeja KP &lt;jeeja.kp@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Takashi Iwai &lt;tiwai@suse.de&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:48270 TEST=with the patch applied, the audio subsystem is stable. TEST=there are no regressions observed on Lars.  Signed-off-by: Yong Zhi &lt;yzhi@intel.com&gt; Change-Id: I4d645efd1b6294e4a07d353e97945bc12e5a5c5e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/382634 Commit-Ready: Sathya Prakash M R &lt;sathya.prakash.m.r@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Yong Zhi &lt;yong.zhi@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="382634" owner_email="yong.zhi@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/34/382634/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib53a9010f2afdc2ba59369fb145aef4381db30d3" commit="43dd3cb152392f9dc6e3a332e877904e2df7f7ae" commit_message="bdb: Define RSA symbols non-weakly  Defining these symbols weakly causes the output executable to hit segmentation fault because ld chooses *UND* symbols over the definition when they appear in *.a archive:  $ objdump -t build/libvboot_utilbdb.a bdb.o: 0000000000000000 w   *UND* 0000000000000000 bdb_rsa4096_verify ... rsa.o 000000000000061f w F .text 0000000000000111 bdb_rsa4096_verify ...  This happens regardless whether the symbol is referenced or not; or whether the object defining the symbol appears earlier than the reference or not.  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=make runtests  Change-Id: Ib53a9010f2afdc2ba59369fb145aef4381db30d3 Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/387905 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="387905" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/05/387905/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9d66c04e2ed79ab203c54f0a8dad82f32856bbf0" commit="4f23cba7a4ca2344554fd4f2af886d81ee3e6b07" commit_message="power: common: Prevent console spam.  The power state driver would print out the current power state along with its signals everytime a power signal interrupt was fired.  On some systems, a signal may briefly go low and then come back before our chipset module has a chance to notice.  This causes what appears to be duplicate prints.  This commit tries to only print out the current power state when something has actually changed.  If the input power signals or state differs from the last time it checked, then the information will be printed.  BUG=None BRANCH=gru TEST=Find a kevin where PGOOD goes away quite frequently.  Build and flash; Verify that significantly less &quot;power state S0&quot; console spam is emitted. TEST=Verify that all state transitions are still printed.  Change-Id: I9d66c04e2ed79ab203c54f0a8dad82f32856bbf0 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388761 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="388761" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/61/388761/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0873d13b606f3e49b9d055e9dd081d3dacd97c65" commit="bc022721eaa50f18e5779d0c9347550251927e4a" commit_message="Revert &quot;Change debug key signatures&quot;  The lab use test image (non-signed) to run CTS, so we still need to switch key to make a test pass (which blacklist Google's dev key).  This reverts commit b94145a309131f23d49a08dd94fc26247621da65.  TEST=None BUG=b:29915721,b:31373710  Change-Id: I0873d13b606f3e49b9d055e9dd081d3dacd97c65 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388636 Commit-Ready: Victor Hsieh &lt;victorhsieh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Victor Hsieh &lt;victorhsieh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="388636" owner_email="victorhsieh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/36/388636/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia53f6bcc16445c449454c381c889dc4f36a94f9b" commit="630cc5a6889d206dfc7706179dd3c85d0d959d35" commit_message="power: replace deprecated ScopedVector&lt;T&gt;  This CL changes powerd to use vector&lt;unique_ptr&lt;T&gt;&gt; instead of the deprecated ScopedVector&lt;T&gt;.  BUG=chromium:554289 TEST=Build and run unit tests.  Change-Id: Ia53f6bcc16445c449454c381c889dc4f36a94f9b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/388861 Commit-Ready: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="38886